        </div>
      </div>

      <section class="hero">
        <div class="container">
          <div class="tag">JPSC PRELIMS • PAPER 2 • JHARKHAND GK</div>
          <h1>
            JPSC Paper 2:
            <span>Master Jharkhand.</span>
          </h1>
          <p class="hero-text">
            A complete preparation guide for the Jharkhand-focused Preliminary
            paper: syllabus mapping, high-value topics, land laws, history,
            movement, culture, geography, economy, schemes, environment,
            current affairs and PYQ-based preparation.
          </p>

          <div class="meta">
            <span>Updated: 16 August 2026</span>
            <span>•</span>
            <span>Habitat IAS</span>
            <span>•</span>
            <span>Jharkhand Special</span>
          </div>

          <div class="buttons">
            <a class="btn yellow" href="#syllabus">See Syllabus Map ↓</a>
            <a class="btn outline" href="/book/">JPSC PYQ Book →</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="warning-section">
        <div class="container">
          <div class="warning">
            <strong>Use the latest official syllabus:</strong>
            JPSC's official website publishes the syllabus and recruitment
            material for its Combined Civil Services examinations. The detailed
            topic framework below is organised as a preparation guide; the latest
            official notification/syllabus remains the controlling source.
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="stats">
        <div class="container stats-grid">
          <div><b>01</b><span>History</span><p>Jharkhand history, resistance and state formation.</p></div>
          <div><b>02</b><span>Society</span><p>Tribes, identity, culture, literature and institutions.</p></div>
          <div><b>03</b><span>Economy</span><p>Development, industries, policies and schemes.</p></div>
          <div><b>04</b><span>Law + Environment</span><p>Land laws, forests, climate and disaster management.</p></div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="content">
        <div class="container layout">
          <aside class="toc">
            <strong>ON THIS PAGE</strong>
            <a href="#paper">Paper 2 at a glance</a>
            <a href="#syllabus">Syllabus map</a>
            <a href="#history">History</a>
            <a href="#movement">Jharkhand Movement</a>
            <a href="#identity">Society & identity</a>
            <a href="#culture">Culture & literature</a>
            <a href="#geography">Geography</a>
            <a href="#laws">Land laws</a>
            <a href="#economy">Economy & industries</a>
            <a href="#schemes">Schemes</a>
            <a href="#environment">Environment</a>
            <a href="#current">Current affairs</a>
            <a href="#pyq">PYQ strategy</a>
            <a href="#plan">90-day plan</a>
            <a href="#mistakes">Mistakes</a>
            <a href="#faq">FAQs</a>
          </aside>

          <article>
            <p class="lead">
              If there is one part of JPSC preparation that should never be
              treated as “just another GK chapter,” it is
              <strong>Jharkhand-specific preparation</strong>. The state-focused
              syllabus is broad, interconnected and highly suitable for
              topic-wise PYQ analysis.
            </p>

            <h2 id="paper">1. JPSC Paper 2 at a Glance</h2>

            <div class="paper">
              <div><b>FOCUS</b><strong>Jharkhand</strong><span>State-specific history, society, culture, geography, economy, laws and development.</span></div>
              <div><b>METHOD</b><strong>Objective MCQs</strong><span>Preparation should combine factual recall with conceptual and statement-based understanding.</span></div>
              <div><b>BEST RESOURCE</b><strong>PYQs</strong><span>Previous questions show how broad state material becomes examination questions.</span></div>
              <div><b>BEST REVISION</b><strong>Short notes</strong><span>Build compact district, law, culture, geography and history revision sheets.</span></div>
            </div>

            <div class="formula">
              <strong>Jharkhand Paper = Static Knowledge + State Current Affairs + PYQs + Repeated Revision</strong>
              <span>Do not prepare these as four disconnected subjects.</span>
            </div>

            <h2 id="syllabus">2. Complete Jharkhand Syllabus Map</h2>

            <div class="syllabus">
              <div><b>01</b><strong>History of Jharkhand</strong><span>Regional history, dynasties, colonial developments and major historical events.</span></div>
              <div><b>02</b><strong>Jharkhand Movement</strong><span>Tribal and regional movements, leaders, organisations and statehood.</span></div>
              <div><b>03</b><strong>Society & Identity</strong><span>Tribes, communities, social, political, religious and economic identities.</span></div>
              <div><b>04</b><strong>Culture</strong><span>Folk traditions, literature, dance, music, instruments and tourism.</span></div>
              <div><b>05</b><strong>Geography</strong><span>Forests, rivers, hills, minerals, climate, districts and resources.</span></div>
              <div><b>06</b><strong>Land Laws</strong><span>CNT, SPT and other relevant state laws and provisions.</span></div>
              <div><b>07</b><strong>Economy</strong><span>Post-independence development, industries, policies and displacement.</span></div>
              <div><b>08</b><strong>Schemes</strong><span>Major state government schemes and sub-schemes.</span></div>
              <div><b>09</b><strong>Environment</strong><span>Forests, wildlife, climate change, mitigation and adaptation.</span></div>
              <div><b>10</b><strong>Disaster Management</strong><span>Jharkhand-specific hazards, preparedness and response.</span></div>
              <div><b>11</b><strong>Education & Sports</strong><span>Important institutions, achievements and state developments.</span></div>
              <div><b>12</b><strong>Current Affairs</strong><span>Major Jharkhand developments linked to static syllabus areas.</span></div>
            </div>

            <h2 id="history">3. History of Jharkhand</h2>

            <p>
              Jharkhand history should be studied as a sequence of political,
              social, tribal, economic and colonial transformations—not as a
              collection of isolated dates.
            </p>

            <div class="history">
              <div><b>EARLY HISTORY</b><span>Important regional references, kingdoms, dynastic developments and historical geography.</span></div>
              <div><b>COLONIAL PERIOD</b><span>British expansion, administrative change, land relations and resistance.</span></div>
              <div><b>TRIBAL RESISTANCE</b><span>Major rebellions, leaders, causes, areas and outcomes.</span></div>
              <div><b>POST-INDEPENDENCE</b><span>Regional political developments and the path toward statehood.</span></div>
            </div>

            <div class="tip">
              <strong>History method:</strong>
              For every movement, make a six-point card:
              <em>leader → community → area → cause → major event → result</em>.
            </div>

            <h2 id="movement">4. Jharkhand Movement & State Formation</h2>

            <p>
              This deserves separate preparation because the movement connects
              history, identity, politics, geography and the eventual creation
              of Jharkhand as a state.
            </p>

            <div class="movement">
              <div><b>BACKGROUND</b><span>Regional identity, tribal society, economic and political concerns.</span></div>
              <div><b>LEADERS</b><span>Important personalities and their organisations.</span></div>
              <div><b>ORGANISATIONS</b><span>Major political and social organisations associated with the movement.</span></div>
              <div><b>DEMAND</b><span>Evolution of the separate-state demand.</span></div>
              <div><b>STATEHOOD</b><span>Political process leading to creation of Jharkhand.</span></div>
            </div>

            <p>
              Do not memorise only names. Link personalities to organisations,
              regions, phases and ideas. This makes factual questions much easier
              to retain.
            </p>

            <h2 id="identity">5. Tribes, Society & Jharkhand Identity</h2>

            <p>
              Prepare tribal and social topics systematically. For important
              communities, create a common template rather than writing random
              facts.
            </p>

            <div class="tribe">
              <div><b>NAME</b><span>Community / tribe.</span></div>
              <div><b>AREA</b><span>Major geographical distribution.</span></div>
              <div><b>LANGUAGE</b><span>Important language/dialect association.</span></div>
              <div><b>CULTURE</b><span>Festivals, traditions, music and social practices.</span></div>
              <div><b>ECONOMY</b><span>Traditional livelihood and contemporary changes.</span></div>
              <div><b>SPECIAL FACT</b><span>Distinctive feature with exam relevance.</span></div>
            </div>

            <p>
              Use the same template for each major tribe/community. This reduces
              revision complexity and helps with comparison questions.
            </p>

            <h2 id="culture">6. Folk Culture, Literature, Dance & Music</h2>

            <div class="culture">
              <div><b>FOLK LITERATURE</b><span>Important traditions, forms, themes and associated communities.</span></div>
              <div><b>FOLK DANCE</b><span>Name, occasion, community and distinguishing features.</span></div>
              <div><b>FOLK MUSIC</b><span>Forms, instruments, performers and cultural context.</span></div>
              <div><b>LANGUAGES</b><span>Regional and tribal languages/literary traditions.</span></div>
              <div><b>AUTHORS</b><span>Important writers and their works.</span></div>
              <div><b>TOURISM</b><span>Natural, archaeological, religious and modern destinations.</span></div>
            </div>

            <div class="tip">
              <strong>Memory technique:</strong>
              Make a “Culture Matrix” with columns for
              <em>name → type → community → region → special feature</em>.
            </div>

            <h2 id="geography">7. Geography of Jharkhand</h2>

            <p>
              Geography is one of the easiest areas to convert into maps and
              visual revision. Keep a physical map of Jharkhand beside your
              notes.
            </p>

            <div class="geography">
              <div><b>PHYSIOGRAPHY</b><span>Plateaus, hills and major physical divisions.</span></div>
              <div><b>RIVERS</b><span>River systems, tributaries, dams and important locations.</span></div>
              <div><b>FORESTS</b><span>Forest regions, types and important protected areas.</span></div>
              <div><b>MINERALS</b><span>Major minerals and their geographical concentration.</span></div>
              <div><b>INDUSTRIES</b><span>Industrial locations and resource linkages.</span></div>
              <div><b>CLIMATE</b><span>Rainfall, temperature, seasons and climate-related issues.</span></div>
              <div><b>AGRICULTURE</b><span>Crops, irrigation and agricultural geography.</span></div>
              <div><b>DISTRICTS</b><span>District-wise important geographical and economic facts.</span></div>
            </div>

            <h2>8. Build a Jharkhand Map Notebook</h2>

            <div class="mapbook">
              <div><b>MAP 01</b><span>Districts + headquarters.</span></div>
              <div><b>MAP 02</b><span>Rivers + dams.</span></div>
              <div><b>MAP 03</b><span>Mineral belts.</span></div>
              <div><b>MAP 04</b><span>Industries.</span></div>
              <div><b>MAP 05</b><span>Forests + wildlife.</span></div>
              <div><b>MAP 06</b><span>Tourist / heritage sites.</span></div>
            </div>

            <h2 id="laws">9. CNT, SPT & Other Jharkhand Land Laws</h2>

            <p>
              Land-related laws are high-responsibility preparation material.
              Do not learn them from random social-media summaries. Use the
              authoritative legal text or a reliable legal reference and
              understand the provisions before converting them into short notes.
            </p>

            <div class="laws">
              <div><b>CNT</b><strong>Chota Nagpur Tenancy</strong><span>Study historical purpose, applicability, key restrictions, terminology and relevant provisions.</span></div>
              <div><b>SPT</b><strong>Santhal Pargana Tenancy</strong><span>Study its regional context, key provisions and distinctions from other tenancy arrangements.</span></div>
              <div><b>OTHER</b><strong>State-specific laws</strong><span>Map other land-related Acts and provisions named in the current syllabus.</span></div>
            </div>

            <div class="warning-box">
              <strong>Legal accuracy rule:</strong>
              Laws can be amended. For examination preparation, always verify
              important provisions against the current statutory text and
              authoritative government/legal sources.
            </div>

            <h2 id="economy">10. Jharkhand Economy & Industrial Development</h2>

            <div class="economy">
              <div><b>POST-1947</b><span>Major phases and features of economic development.</span></div>
              <div><b>MINING</b><span>Major minerals, resource regions and industrial linkages.</span></div>
              <div><b>INDUSTRY</b><span>Major industries, locations and industrial development.</span></div>
              <div><b>POLICY</b><span>Industrial policies and development initiatives.</span></div>
              <div><b>DISPLACEMENT</b><span>Causes, impacts, rehabilitation and policy dimensions.</span></div>
              <div><b>AGRICULTURE</b><span>Farming, livelihoods, irrigation and rural development.</span></div>
            </div>

            <h2 id="schemes">11. Government Schemes & Sub-Schemes</h2>

            <p>
              Do not prepare schemes as a long list of names. Build a table that
              lets you compare purpose, target group and implementing department.
            </p>

            <div class="scheme">
              <div><b>NAME</b><span>Scheme / programme.</span></div>
              <div><b>OBJECTIVE</b><span>What problem does it address?</span></div>
              <div><b>BENEFICIARY</b><span>Who receives the benefit?</span></div>
              <div><b>DEPARTMENT</b><span>Which authority implements it?</span></div>
              <div><b>FEATURE</b><span>One distinctive exam-relevant point.</span></div>
            </div>

            <h2 id="environment">12. Forest, Wildlife & Environment</h2>

            <div class="environment">
              <div><b>FORESTS</b><span>Forest resources, management and conservation.</span></div>
              <div><b>WILDLIFE</b><span>Important protected areas, species and conservation issues.</span></div>
              <div><b>CLIMATE</b><span>Climate change, mitigation and adaptation in the state.</span></div>
              <div><b>MINING IMPACT</b><span>Environmental and developmental dimensions.</span></div>
              <div><b>CONSERVATION</b><span>Institutions, protected areas and community dimensions.</span></div>
            </div>

            <h2>13. Disaster Management in Jharkhand</h2>

            <p>
              Prepare disaster management through a simple risk framework:
              hazard → vulnerability → exposure → preparedness → response →
              recovery.
            </p>

            <div class="disaster">
              <div><b>HAZARD</b><span>What natural or human-induced hazard is involved?</span></div>
              <div><b>LOCATION</b><span>Which parts of Jharkhand are more exposed?</span></div>
              <div><b>IMPACT</b><span>What are the social, economic and environmental consequences?</span></div>
              <div><b>RESPONSE</b><span>Which institutions and measures are involved?</span></div>
            </div>

            <h2 id="current">14. Jharkhand Current Affairs</h2>

            <p>
              Current affairs should update your static notes, not replace them.
              Every major state event should be connected to one syllabus topic.
            </p>

            <div class="current">
              <div><b>POLICY</b><span>New government decisions.</span></div>
              <div><b>SCHEME</b><span>New/modified programmes.</span></div>
              <div><b>ECONOMY</b><span>Projects, industries and investments.</span></div>
              <div><b>ENVIRONMENT</b><span>Forests, wildlife and climate events.</span></div>
              <div><b>CULTURE</b><span>Heritage, festivals, awards and literature.</span></div>
              <div><b>PEOPLE</b><span>Important appointments, awards and personalities.</span></div>
            </div>

            <h2 id="pyq">15. PYQ Strategy for Paper 2</h2>

            <p>
              The biggest advantage of topic-wise PYQs is that they transform a
              huge Jharkhand syllabus into observable question patterns. Public
              PYQ repositories also show that multiple JPSC cycles are available
              for comparison, including recent papers and older Preliminary
              papers. citeturn0search4
            </p>

            <div class="pyq-cycle">
              <div><b>1. ATTEMPT</b><span>Answer without notes.</span></div>
              <i>→</i>
              <div><b>2. MAP</b><span>Assign the syllabus topic.</span></div>
              <i>→</i>
              <div><b>3. STUDY</b><span>Read the underlying concept.</span></div>
              <i>→</i>
              <div><b>4. RECORD</b><span>Save the important point.</span></div>
              <i>→</i>
              <div><b>5. REVISE</b><span>Return during revision.</span></div>
              <i>→</i>
              <div><b>6. RETEST</b><span>Check retention.</span></div>
            </div>

            <div class="conversion">
              <div>
                <span>HABITAT IAS • JPSC PYQ DECODED</span>
                <h2>Prepare Jharkhand topic by topic.</h2>
                <p>
                  Use topic-wise PYQs to connect the enormous Jharkhand syllabus
                  with actual JPSC question patterns and targeted revision.
                </p>
              </div>
              <div class="cta-buttons">
                <a class="btn yellow" href="/book/">Explore PYQ Book →</a>
                <a class="btn outline" href="/mock-tests/free-gs/">Free Mock →</a>
              </div>
            </div>

            <h2>16. High-Priority Revision Order</h2>

            <div class="priority">
              <div><b>PHASE 1</b><strong>History + Movement</strong><span>Build the chronological foundation.</span></div>
              <div><b>PHASE 2</b><strong>Geography</strong><span>Map districts, rivers, minerals and forests.</span></div>
              <div><b>PHASE 3</b><strong>Society + Culture</strong><span>Tribes, identity, literature, dance and music.</span></div>
              <div><b>PHASE 4</b><strong>Laws + Economy</strong><span>Land laws, industries, policies and development.</span></div>
              <div><b>PHASE 5</b><strong>Schemes + Environment</strong><span>Government programmes, forests, wildlife and climate.</span></div>
              <div><b>PHASE 6</b><strong>Current Affairs</strong><span>Update all static sections with recent developments.</span></div>
            </div>

            <h2>17. The Jharkhand Fact Card</h2>

            <p>
              Create one reusable template for every important fact. This makes
              revision dramatically faster.
            </p>

            <div class="fact">
              <div><b>WHAT?</b><span>Name / event / institution.</span></div>
              <div><b>WHERE?</b><span>District / region.</span></div>
              <div><b>WHEN?</b><span>Date / period.</span></div>
              <div><b>WHO?</b><span>Leader / community / organisation.</span></div>
              <div><b>WHY?</b><span>Historical or contemporary significance.</span></div>
              <div><b>PYQ?</b><span>Has JPSC tested a related concept?</span></div>
            </div>

            <h2 id="plan">18. 90-Day Jharkhand Preparation Plan</h2>

            <div class="months">
              <div>
                <span>DAYS 1–30</span>
                <strong>Foundation</strong>
                <p>History, movement, geography, tribes and society. Start topic-wise PYQs immediately.</p>
              </div>
              <div>
                <span>DAYS 31–60</span>
                <strong>Depth</strong>
                <p>Culture, literature, laws, economy, industries, schemes and environment.</p>
              </div>
              <div>
                <span>DAYS 61–90</span>
                <strong>Testing</strong>
                <p>Revision, mixed Jharkhand MCQs, full tests, error analysis and current-affairs integration.</p>
              </div>
            </div>

            <h2>19. Weekly Jharkhand Study Routine</h2>

            <div class="week">
              <div><b>MON</b><span>History</span></div>
              <div><b>TUE</b><span>Movement + Society</span></div>
              <div><b>WED</b><span>Geography</span></div>
              <div><b>THU</b><span>Culture + Literature</span></div>
              <div><b>FRI</b><span>Laws + Economy</span></div>
              <div><b>SAT</b><span>Schemes + Environment</span></div>
              <div><b>SUN</b><span>PYQ + Mock + Revision</span></div>
            </div>

            <h2>20. How to Analyse a Paper 2 Mock</h2>

            <div class="analysis">
              <div><b>KNOWLEDGE ERROR</b><span>You never studied the fact.</span></div>
              <div><b>CONCEPT ERROR</b><span>You misunderstood the topic.</span></div>
              <div><b>MEMORY ERROR</b><span>You studied but forgot it.</span></div>
              <div><b>CONFUSION ERROR</b><span>You mixed two similar facts.</span></div>
              <div><b>CARELESS ERROR</b><span>You knew the answer but misread.</span></div>
              <div><b>GUESSING ERROR</b><span>You chose without enough evidence.</span></div>
            </div>

            <div class="conversion">
              <div>
                <span>HABITAT IAS • MOCK TESTS</span>
                <h2>Test your Jharkhand preparation.</h2>
                <p>
                  A mock should tell you which part of the syllabus needs repair,
                  not merely give you a score.
                </p>
              </div>
              <div class="cta-buttons">
                <a class="btn yellow" href="/mock-tests/free-gs/">Attempt Free Mock →</a>
                <a class="btn outline" href="/mock-tests/">View Mock Tests →</a>
              </div>
            </div>

            <h2 id="mistakes">21. Biggest Paper 2 Preparation Mistakes</h2>

            <div class="mistakes">
              <div><b>01</b><span>Studying Jharkhand only during the final month.</span></div>
              <div><b>02</b><span>Using one generic GK book as the complete Jharkhand source.</span></div>
              <div><b>03</b><span>Memorising tribe names without geography or cultural context.</span></div>
